 "description": "The shade-loving fir of the Olympics' middle slopes, 30-50 m here, a dense, dark, narrow spire on a smooth, pale-grey trunk dotted with resin blisters. Its needles are a deep glossy green above and brilliant silvery-white beneath, so the forest flashes silver when wind turns the boughs.",
 "season_notes": {
  "winter": "Evergreen under deep, wet snow; the dense tiers hold it.",
  "spring": "Shoots break late in pale green tufts; red pollen cones under the branches.",
  "summer": "Upright, resinous purple cones 8-10 cm sit on the top branches.",
  "fall": "The cones fall apart on the branch, leaving bare spikes; seedlings carpet the shaded duff."
